@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Resolution book development copy
+
+Upstream: https://github.com/gerby-project/gerby-website
+
+The `resolution-book` branch starts from upstream commit `01b11bbbbd1a910bc997eb3d53bd1cd8c8de8652`.
+Continuous readers, bibliography and download views, source sidenotes, citations, and Resolution reading styles.
+
+This is a private standalone GitHub repository; upstream history is preserved.
+The original licenses continue to apply. The website also contains adapted
+ForumMagnum code, whose source, modification notes and GPL-3.0 license are
+included in `third_party/forum-magnum/` and the served static assets.
+
+The book and its build entry point live in `lean/hironaka/book/` in the
+Resolution monorepo. That branch records this repository's exact commit and
+Git tree, and carries a binary-capable patch against the upstream revision.
+The build verifies the reconstructed tree, allowing CI and colleagues to build
+without separate credentials for this private repository. After updating this
+branch, refresh the book's patch and pin together with `tools/lock_renderer.py`.
+
+The website requires `GERBY_CONFIG_FILE` to point to the book's instance
+configuration. There is no deployment configured here.
