+{% block body %}<h2>About this reconstruction</h2>
+<p>This is an independent mathematical reconstruction of the algebraic and analytic resolution library, presented using the actual Gerby software used by the Stacks Project.</p>
+<p>Local tags identify statements in this text. They are not tags assigned by the Stacks Project. External Stacks references link to <a href="https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/">the Stacks Project</a>; formal source references point to the <a href="https://github.com/resolutionorg/hironaka/tree/29f3df958d023a944de44adcca91a18e5dabec88">Resolution Lean repository at revision <code>29f3df958d023a944de44adcca91a18e5dabec88</code></a>.</p>
+<p>The <a href="/tag/R000">introduction</a> records the mathematical scope. The <a href="/download/manuscript.tex">local LaTeX source</a> contains the complete reconstructed manuscript. This is a working reconstruction; the prose requires mathematical review. The web software does not certify the prose proof.</p>
+<p>This instance runs <a href="https://gerby-project.github.io/">Gerby</a>, the open-source system developed by Pieter Belmans and Raymond Cheng: its <a href="https://github.com/gerby-project/plastex/tree/a75473f890db3d21e3bf76430c5c1ffc0661a69a">plasTeX Gerby renderer</a> and <a href="https://github.com/gerby-project/gerby-website/tree/01b11bbbbd1a910bc997eb3d53bd1cd8c8de8652">Gerby website application</a>, with documented local compatibility and instance patches.</p>
+<p>Typography and colors follow <a href="https://resolution.org/">Resolution</a>: Spectral, Inter, IBM Plex Mono, white paper, dark ink, and a slate accent. The reading layout is inspired by LessWrong. Its progress-line interpolation and contents scaling are adapted from <a href="https://github.com/ForumMagnum/ForumMagnum/tree/a1665ead02e2c00647c098797979c4c994980673/packages/lesswrong/components/posts/TableOfContents">ForumMagnum</a>, with the <a href="/static/third-party/forum-magnum/LICENSE">GPL version 3 license</a>, original sources, and modification notes distributed with this edition. Gerby continues to render and serve the mathematical text.</p>
 {% endblock %}
